# RECOVERY NOTE (Sprint 17.3): deliberately does NOT ignore gradlew,
# gradlew.bat, or gradle-wrapper.jar — Sprint 17.2's own root-cause
# finding was that this project's Gradle scaffold (INCLUDING the
# wrapper) had never been committed at all. Ignoring the wrapper
# again here would silently reintroduce the exact same bug.
/.gradle
/captures/
local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/
key.properties

# PHASE G — RELEASE SIGNING. NEVER COMMIT KEY MATERIAL.
#
# `signing.properties` holds the keystore path and three passwords and is read
# by app/build.gradle. `signing.properties.example` IS committed (note the
# negation below) because it is the template and carries the keytool command.
#
# The keystore extensions are ignored by pattern rather than by name so that a
# developer who calls theirs `abny-upload-2027.jks` is covered too. There is no
# safe filename for a private key in a repository.
signing.properties
!signing.properties.example
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pepk
